> 
> Basically you have two choices; the easier is without installing that font,
> eg. starting xterm like
> 
> xterm -fn /path/to/the/vga.pcf
> 
> or you can install the font (this is the manual way, i'm pretty sure
> there are programs that automate some or all of this):
> 
> 1) copy the vga.pcf to X fonts directory, which could be something like
> /usr/share/fonts/X11/misc/
> 2) go to that dir, and do 'mkfontdir'
> 3) do 'xset fp rehash'
> 4) verify the font is seen by X, by doing 'xlsfonts'
> (or rather, 'xlsfonts | grep vga')
> 5) use your terminal's configuration abilities so the terminal uses the
> vga font.
> 
> googling also should find some help for this.

